    <statement><p>The figure below shows <m>f</m>.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap5Sec4__Q03-image-1.png" width="33%">
<shortdescription>graph of a piecewise linear function</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A piecewise linear function.  The first line segment goes from <m>(0,-1)</m> to <m>(3,-1)</m>; the second line segment goes from <m>(3,-1)</m> to <m>(5,1)</m>; the third line segment goes from <m>(5,1)</m> to <m>(6,0)</m>.</p>
</description>
</image>
<p><em>(Click on the graph for a larger version.)</em></p>
<p>If <m>F'=f</m> and <m>F(0)=0</m>,
find <m>F(b)</m> for <m>b=</m>1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and fill these values in the
following table.</p>
<tabular bottom="minor" left="minor" top="major" valign="top">
